course: dictionary
lesson: 4161
title: Many meanings of go
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Go» is one of the most common words in English, and it has many meanings. Most of the time, the sentence tells you which one you need. «Go to school» means move from one place to another. «The cups go in the cupboard» means they belong in the cupboard.
explain: Look at the words around «go». «The car won't go» means the car won't work, and «How did the test go?» means how did it happen. Ask yourself: what would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence to see if it makes sense.
explain: Some meanings are casual, like everyday chat. «And he goes, "no way!"» means he says it. «Have a go» means try, and «on the go» means busy. In a formal text, the same idea might use a different word, such as «depart» or «proceed».
explain: «Go» can also mean turn. «It's my go» means it is my turn to play. In a game, a go is one turn, so you can work out the meaning from the game around it.
fact: «Go» can mean move from one place to another, as in «go to school».
fact: «Go» can mean fit or belong in a place, as in «the cups go in the cupboard».
fact: «Go» can mean become, as in «go red» or «go quiet».
fact: A «go» is a turn or a try, as in «it's my go» or «have a go».
fact: «Gonna» is a casual way of writing «going to», and «on the go» means busy.
exercise: «If something ever goes wrong in the air, two tough recorders called the black box help investigators find out why.» What does goes wrong mean here? | *Something stops working the way it should | Something is taken to the shop | Something moves very fast | Something gets very loud
exercise: Jade says, «It's my go.» What does go mean in her sentence? | A place to visit | A shout of surprise | A kind of food | *Her turn
exercise: Find the casual word that means «going to» in this sentence: «Gonna play outside after lunch.» | after | outside | play | *gonna
test: «The cups go in the cupboard.» What does go mean here? | To run very fast | To fall asleep | *To belong or fit in a place | To shout loudly
test: «The sky will go dark soon.» What does go mean here? | Fall | Eat | *Become | Shine
exam: «The train will go at noon.» In a formal text, which word could replace go here? | hide | sleep | forget | *depart
